1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:06,089
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

2
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:10,760
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

3
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:13,012
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

4
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:16,182
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

5
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:22,021
Samir: I think it is time to go
visit our prisoners.

6
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:25,442
We will make them tell us
who Belladonna is.

7
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:27,652
[thumps & squeals]

8
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:28,570
- Others: Hey!
- [growling & grunting]

9
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:30,613
Ibyang: Tatoy has no
friend anymore.

10
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:31,948
That’s sad.

11
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:34,367
We haven't seen each other in
a long time, so it's like--

12
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:35,910
Atoy: You know? We drifted apart.

13
00:00:35,994 --> 00:00:38,872
Uno Alcaraz has been moved
to a regular room.

14
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:39,956
Let's go,

15
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:40,790
because there are people

16
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:41,875
who want to talk to him.

17
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:43,668
Who? Atoy?

18
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:45,211
Shugo: They didn't say.

19
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:48,840
Tell me who was hired to rescue
the Belladonna.

20
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:50,467
I don't know.

21
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:51,092
[electric buzzing]

22
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:51,718
[gunshot]

23
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,136
The Firefighter.

24
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:54,721
That's Uno Alcaraz.

25
00:00:54,804 --> 00:00:57,348
Then we must go right
now and get him.

26
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:58,725
I need to talk to Uno.

27
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:03,146
- We're now the official BFFs, Ja-Ha-Byang!
- What?

28
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:04,647
Samir: But we have to be very careful.

29
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:06,441
We cannot draw too much attention.

30
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,192
I'm so dirty!

31
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:08,193
Let's switch jackets!

32
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:08,985
This is disgusting!

33
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:10,195
Yes, sir.

34
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:11,613
Nurse: He's in 415 now.

35
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:13,615
But you can't just visit on a whim.

36
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:15,033
Atoy: We'll put Uno on this.

37
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:16,826
We'll pretend we're sending
him to get a CT scan,

38
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,203
then we'll take him straight
downstairs.

39
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:20,080
That's Atoy.

40
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:20,789
Samir: Uhm, we are here
to transfer

41
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:23,708
the patient to another floor.

42
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:24,876
[groans]

43
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,044
ELIAS: It was Atoy whom I saw,

44
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:27,128
I'm not mistaken.

45
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:27,921
[music continues]

46
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:28,713
[bullet whizzing]

47
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:29,839
[groaning]

48
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:32,091
[groaning]

49
00:01:32,675 --> 00:01:33,968
We need him alive! Let's go!

50
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:35,512
Hey! Let go of her.

51
00:01:35,595 --> 00:01:36,221
[thumps & thuds]

52
00:01:36,304 --> 00:01:36,805
[grunts & groans]

53
00:01:36,888 --> 00:01:39,182
NURSE: Someone is shooting in
patient Alcaraz’s room!

54
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:41,559
The cop who was guarding
him is already dead.

55
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,144
Call the police!

56
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,188
ELIAS: I'm a police officer,
I just remembered.

57
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:54,906
[action music playing]

58
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:12,715
[footsteps tapping]

59
00:02:31,234 --> 00:02:33,069
Stop! We're police!

60
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:36,573
[ominous music playing]

61
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:43,413
[gunshots]

62
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:46,207
[gunshots]

63
00:02:48,042 --> 00:02:54,340
[action music playing]
[gunshots]

64
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:58,720
[gunshots]

65
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:09,314
Artem, take the fire exit.

66
00:03:09,397 --> 00:03:10,815
We need Uno Alacaraz.

67
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:11,941
I'll stay here and handle
these two.

68
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,109
Go!

69
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:14,360
[bullets whizzing]

70
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:16,112
[gunshots]

71
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:17,739
[bullets whizzing]

72
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:19,449
[grunts]

73
00:03:23,745 --> 00:03:24,662
[gunshots]

74
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:30,084
[breathes heavily]

75
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:39,302
[sneaky music playing]

76
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:44,974
[music fades]

77
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,810
No more bullets!

78
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:48,686
[smirks]

79
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:50,980
I've got some bullets
for your face!

80
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:56,361
[rock music playing]

81
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:13,378
[music fades]

82
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:15,129
[gunshots]

83
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:17,423
[tense music playing]

84
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:21,302
[bullets whizzing]

85
00:04:21,386 --> 00:04:23,054
[music continues]

86
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:24,889
[music swells]

87
00:04:24,973 --> 00:04:26,516
[music fades]

88
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:31,562
[theme music playing]

89
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:34,482
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪

90
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:39,445
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

91
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:42,240
♪ Wait a moment, Mister Tailor ♪

92
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:44,409
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

93
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:45,576
♪ The hole in my polo

94
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:47,787
that's right under the armpit ♪

95
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:49,956
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

96
00:04:50,039 --> 00:04:51,499
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

97
00:04:51,582 --> 00:04:53,459
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

98
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:58,006
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

99
00:04:58,089 --> 00:04:58,715
[gunshots]

100
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:00,466
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

101
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,719
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

102
00:05:02,802 --> 00:05:04,429
[music swells]

103
00:05:05,847 --> 00:05:07,932
[music fades]

104
00:05:09,517 --> 00:05:11,477
What? Are you okay?

105
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:12,603
You're so heavy, Sir.

106
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:15,106
[groans]

107
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:17,859
[tense music playing]

108
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:25,450
[bullets whizzing]

109
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,201
[music continues]

110
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:29,829
[thuds]

111
00:05:29,912 --> 00:05:31,748
[thumping & thudding]

112
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:34,000
[music continues]

113
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:39,547
[thumps]

114
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:42,467
[music swells]

115
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:45,386
[grunting & groaning]

116
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:50,141
[thumping & thudding]

117
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:53,144
[grunting & groaning]

118
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:57,815
[thumping & thudding]

119
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:02,779
[music swells]

120
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:12,288
[grunts]

121
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:14,540
[thumps]

122
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:16,626
[grunting]

123
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:20,213
[music continues]

124
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:30,473
[bullets whizzing]

125
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:32,141
[music swells]

126
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:33,142
[music fades]

127
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:35,144
Oop!

128
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:35,978
Stop!

129
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:38,356
[ominous music playing]

130
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:39,690
Who are you?

131
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:44,362
Face this way, take
off that mask!

132
00:06:46,072 --> 00:06:49,117
[music swells]

133
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:52,328
[tense music playing]

134
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:54,997
SHUGO: Sir!

135
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:56,332
What happened?

136
00:06:57,959 --> 00:07:01,045
[rock music playing]

137
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:05,758
[hissing]

138
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:09,512
[groaning]

139
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:17,854
[suspicious music playing]

140
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:22,442
[music swells]

141
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:38,207
MAN: Let's eat, bro.

142
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:40,626
[music fades]

143
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:47,467
[tense music playing]

144
00:07:49,677 --> 00:07:51,637
[car engine revving]

145
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:55,475
[music continues]

146
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:59,645
[thudding]
[groaning]

147
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:16,412
[music swells]

148
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:19,207
You're so stubborn, Uno.

149
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:23,044
[music continues]

150
00:08:23,794 --> 00:08:25,963
[music fades]

151
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:28,132
[muffled chattering]

152
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:29,342
[exclaims]

153
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:31,511
So many clubs,
oh my god.

154
00:08:31,594 --> 00:08:34,138
Dance club! Artsy!

155
00:08:34,222 --> 00:08:36,182
There's-- there's cooking
too!

156
00:08:36,265 --> 00:08:38,601
Earth savers, science club.

157
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:39,560
- Oh my god.
- Earth savers?

158
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:41,020
Hey, cooking club!

159
00:08:41,103 --> 00:08:42,438
We need to have
a club!

160
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:43,814
We'll meet new friends!

161
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:45,691
But we're still solid!

162
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,360
Ja-Ha-Byang forever!

163
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:48,778
The Ja-Ha-Byang trio!

164
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:51,614
Oh, let's just join the…

165
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:52,573
science club!

166
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:54,534
But I'm not good
at science.

167
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:56,619
Exactly--

168
00:08:56,702 --> 00:08:57,203
Ah, something else then.

169
00:08:57,286 --> 00:09:00,122
[lively chatter]

170
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,541
Let's join the dance club!

171
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:02,583
Let’s join the dance club.

172
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:04,710
Hi, I'm Leighton!

173
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:07,672
I'm the dance club president.

174
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:09,173
Are you joining?

175
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:10,383
Both: Yes!

176
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:11,217
Ah, yes!

177
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,760
LEIGHTON: Perfect!

178
00:09:12,843 --> 00:09:14,095
You need to audition as a trio.

179
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:15,805
What kind of dance?

180
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:18,349
Anything. You choose.

181
00:09:18,432 --> 00:09:19,934
You have to do well in
the audition, okay.

182
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:21,894
You have to wow us.

183
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,981
If I were you, I'd practice right away.

184
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:26,607
Game?

185
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:27,567
BOTH: Game!

186
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:28,317
Game.

187
00:09:28,401 --> 00:09:29,944
Good luck to you!

188
00:09:30,027 --> 00:09:30,736
Good luck!

189
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:31,529
Mmm-hmm, yes.

190
00:09:31,612 --> 00:09:33,239
Thank you.

191
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:33,864
[music fades]

192
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:34,699
Brother!

193
00:09:35,783 --> 00:09:37,159
Brother, what happened
to you?

194
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,119
[car door closes]

195
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:39,579
Oh, there's blood.

196
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:42,081
Give me the…
first aid kit.

197
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,084
Okay.

198
00:09:46,043 --> 00:09:47,712
What happened to you?

199
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:48,921
Mmm, yeah.

200
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:50,423
[music continues]

201
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:52,883
It's okay, it's not that bad.

202
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,218
Okay, thank you.

203
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:56,345
[groans]

204
00:09:56,429 --> 00:09:57,471
There.

205
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:58,598
Thanks.

206
00:09:58,681 --> 00:10:00,182
[heavy music playing]

207
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:00,975
Wait.

208
00:10:01,058 --> 00:10:02,852
[music continues]

209
00:10:02,935 --> 00:10:04,770
Brother, what about Uno?

210
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:06,897
I didn't see him.

211
00:10:07,523 --> 00:10:09,233
I really hope he managed
to escape.

212
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:09,900
That's right.

213
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,277
I hope so too.

214
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,154
Don't tell Audrey what
happened, okay.

215
00:10:13,237 --> 00:10:14,363
Okay?

216
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:15,448
Yes, Brother. Okay, okay.

217
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:18,534
[phone ringing]

218
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:19,952
Atoy on the phone: Hello?

219
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:23,581
Atoy, I'm with Oscar at the
hospital now.

220
00:10:23,664 --> 00:10:24,749
[heavy music playing]

221
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:27,960
He was stabbed while
saving me.

222
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:32,423
[music continues]

223
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,053
Oscar…

224
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:41,599
thank you again for
saving me.

225
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,936
If you hadn't come…

226
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:48,105
who knows what would have
happened to me.

227
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:50,733
Just call me Oscar, and…

228
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:53,027
maybe it was just right
place, right time.

229
00:10:54,111 --> 00:10:54,862
[sighs]

230
00:10:55,863 --> 00:10:57,281
Thank you, really.

231
00:10:57,365 --> 00:10:58,783
[music continues]

232
00:10:58,866 --> 00:11:00,451
Uhm, so? Ah--

233
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:02,370
I just need to take care
of something

234
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:04,163
so you can be discharged.

235
00:11:05,706 --> 00:11:06,999
I'll see you later.

236
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:11,087
[music continues]

237
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:15,007
Well, ready?

238
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:16,175
Of course!

239
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:17,802
Ibyang, ready?

240
00:11:18,594 --> 00:11:19,178
You can do this.

241
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:21,555
Okay. We can do
this, guys!

242
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:23,891
[hip-hop upbeat music playing]

243
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:26,727
And 5, 6, 7, 8!

244
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:29,313
1 and 2, 1 and 2.

245
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:32,400
1 and 2, 1 and 2.

246
00:11:32,483 --> 00:11:35,403
JANINE: 1, 2. 1, 2.

247
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:38,447
Single, single. Double, double. There.

248
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:41,325
Single, single. Double, double.

249
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:44,286
Then 1, 2, 3, 4.

250
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:48,916
1, 2, 3, 4. Then, foot.
Then 1…

251
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,544
1, 2…

252
00:11:51,627 --> 00:11:52,586
[music continues]

253
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,255
1, 2…

254
00:11:54,755 --> 00:11:55,881
It's done.

255
00:11:57,591 --> 00:11:58,592
Ibyang.

256
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:00,177
Ibyang, what now?

257
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:02,972
What's wrong with you?

258
00:12:03,055 --> 00:12:03,764
[music fades]

259
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:05,057
Sorry, Janine.

260
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:09,520
I can't keep up with hip-hop!

261
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:10,563
Can't we just do…

262
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:12,815
Tinikling?

263
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:14,525
That's so old school.

264
00:12:15,609 --> 00:12:17,194
It's not Language Week,
you know!

265
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:18,821
That's right.

266
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:21,740
You can clearly see that--

267
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:23,284
President Leighton.

268
00:12:23,909 --> 00:12:25,286
Look at what they’re wearing

269
00:12:25,369 --> 00:12:28,164
and their dance, it's modern.

270
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:30,332
So, we should be
modern too,

271
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:32,126
our dance should be
modern too.

272
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:33,919
You can do this, Ibyang.

273
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:35,880
If you don't know the steps,

274
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,465
I'll teach you, promise.

275
00:12:37,548 --> 00:12:38,757
This is easy. Okay?

276
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:40,217
Just listen.

277
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:44,138
5, 6, 7, 8.

278
00:12:44,221 --> 00:12:47,725
1, down and 2, down, that's it.

279
00:12:47,808 --> 00:12:51,937
Then, 1 and 2, down.

280
00:12:52,354 --> 00:12:53,355
Are you sure you can manage?

281
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:54,023
Oscar: Mmm-hmm.

282
00:12:54,106 --> 00:12:56,233
[Audrey sighs]

283
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:58,027
Atoy.

284
00:12:58,110 --> 00:12:58,944
[sighs]

285
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:01,155
How are you?

286
00:13:01,238 --> 00:13:02,531
I'm okay.

287
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,366
Ah, he's the only one
who got hurt.

288
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:06,619
Bro, how are you?

289
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,120
I'm okay.

290
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:11,207
Audrey told me what
happened.

291
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:13,542
Thank you, okay.

292
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:16,003
Oh. You're welcome, buddy.

293
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:18,714
Uhm, buddy…

294
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:20,883
by the way, I want to…

295
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,469
apologize to you for…

296
00:13:23,552 --> 00:13:26,388
what I did during the-- the
drinking session.

297
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:28,641
Sorry, to you, to all of you
who were there.

298
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:30,184
It's so embarrassing, really.

299
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:31,769
Atoy: It's nothing.

300
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:33,687
Don't worry about that,

301
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:35,064
I'll take care of them.

302
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:37,107
Yes, buddy.
Please tell them I’m sorry, okay.

303
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:38,234
I’m really sorry.

304
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:39,276
I'll take care of that.

305
00:13:40,778 --> 00:13:42,196
So what? Where will you
stay now?

306
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:43,989
It's okay, don't--

307
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:45,157
don't worry about that.

308
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:47,076
OSCAR: Uhm…

309
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:49,495
[pensive music playing]

310
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:53,499
[liquor slopping]

311
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:55,793
[mysterious music playing]

312
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:56,710
[thuds]

313
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:02,758
Samir…

314
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:06,428
who did this to you?

315
00:14:06,512 --> 00:14:08,055
A policeman.

316
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:12,935
He, uhm, interrupted my fight
with a surgeon.

317
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:17,398
Who I know was Anthony Padua.

318
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:19,108
Anthony Padua.

319
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:21,735
Atoy again and again?

320
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:24,780
We must kill that guy.

321
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:25,781
He's a pest.

322
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:30,494
First, we must handle
Uno Alcaraz.

323
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:32,454
He knows who Belladonna is.

324
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:36,625
That is our focus.
Okay?

325
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,754
And then, we will take
care of Atoy.

326
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:43,173
Don't worry.

327
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:45,759
He will have his day.

328
00:14:45,843 --> 00:14:49,096
[tense music playing]

329
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:51,932
Oscar, wait.

330
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:56,520
If you have nowhere else to stay…

331
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:59,064
maybe you'd like…

332
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:01,317
to stay with us for now?

333
00:15:02,776 --> 00:15:03,611
Huh?

334
00:15:04,612 --> 00:15:06,530
Wait, ah-- I thou-- I thought--

335
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:07,948
I thought I wasn't allowed there?

336
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:09,325
Right? I thought you didn't like me?

337
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,951
No, no, no. It's--

338
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:14,330
it's the least I could do, to
make it up to you.

339
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:16,540
For wrongly accusing you

340
00:15:16,624 --> 00:15:18,667
and for you saving me.

341
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:23,672
I was wrong about
you, Oscar.

342
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:26,759
Audrey: Atoy is right.

343
00:15:28,385 --> 00:15:29,720
You're a good person.

344
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:32,806
I-- I want it.

345
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:34,850
If-- if it's okay with you, buddy?

346
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,185
I'm too embarrassed around
you now.

347
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:38,312
[chuckles softly]

348
00:15:38,812 --> 00:15:39,897
Of course.

349
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:40,731
Would I say no to you?

350
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:45,903
[pensive music playing]

351
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:52,660
I'm telling you, My Loves.

352
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:56,580
You have nothing to be jealous
of about Jesabel.

353
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:57,748
She's not my type, okay.

354
00:15:58,290 --> 00:15:59,333
You're the one who's…

355
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:00,960
the needle to my thread.

356
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:02,336
Promise, huh?

357
00:16:02,419 --> 00:16:04,672
Of course. Why won’t you
believe me.

358
00:16:04,755 --> 00:16:06,548
Do you want me to buy out
all the kikiam here

359
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:07,800
and all the fish balls here,

360
00:16:07,883 --> 00:16:10,052
just to prove my love to you,

361
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:11,720
my metal love.

362
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:13,847
My love that lasts.

363
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:16,976
[giggling]

364
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:19,979
Yes! Promise, I saw Oscar
with my eyes,

365
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:21,939
throwing punches like
that nonstop!

366
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:23,399
And he kept missing too!

367
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:25,526
Well, Brother Atoy is so good
at dodging punches!

368
00:16:25,609 --> 00:16:26,485
- [chuckles]
- Yes.

369
00:16:26,568 --> 00:16:28,654
That's why Oscar walked out!

370
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:32,700
As if Atoy would chase after him.

371
00:16:32,783 --> 00:16:33,659
Hmm, so…

372
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:34,910
ignored.

373
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:36,745
He was ignored, he
wasn't chased.

374
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:38,205
Yes.

375
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:41,834
And besides, he can't come
back here,

376
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:42,918
he's no longer welcome.

377
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,545
After what he did to Atoy?

378
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:46,213
He's crossed out, canceled,

379
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:47,840
persona non grata.

380
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:48,632
[chuckles]

381
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:49,842
- Nestor: Emerson!
- Oh?

382
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:51,844
Guess who came back.

383
00:16:51,927 --> 00:16:52,803
Who?

384
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:54,513
- Oscar.
- Huh?

385
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:55,764
What?

386
00:16:56,348 --> 00:16:58,017
He just left last night.

387
00:16:58,392 --> 00:16:59,476
T-Bak: Mmm-mmm.

388
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:02,479
Oh, surely he begged,

389
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:03,480
walked on his knees.

390
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:05,816
And then Atoy took pity. Mmm.

391
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:09,486
Atoy is really so weak sometimes.

392
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,280
That's not really how it
happened, though.

393
00:17:11,363 --> 00:17:12,781
They made up, and
that's it.

394
00:17:13,991 --> 00:17:15,826
What happened was intense.
Really?

395
00:17:15,909 --> 00:17:17,661
Then you and Oscar might
as well be together!

396
00:17:18,912 --> 00:17:21,206
Wait! My Loves!

397
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:22,499
What is this? It’s not--

398
00:17:22,583 --> 00:17:23,292
Sir Nestor, geez.

399
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:24,501
Because of your news,

400
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:26,211
we got disturbed, look.

401
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,213
But are you sure?

402
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:31,884
Why did Atoy let that
troublemaker come back?

403
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:34,511
[sneaky music playing]

404
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:35,804
My Loves!

405
00:17:37,097 --> 00:17:38,223
The--

406
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:39,391
Buy me food.

407
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:40,517
I don't have money, eh.

408
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:42,102
[music fades]

409
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:44,938
And 5, 6, 7, 8.

410
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:48,317
[hip-hop upbeat music playing]

411
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:52,321
Single, single. Double, double.

412
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:53,363
Single--

413
00:17:56,742 --> 00:17:57,534
[music fades]

414
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,079
What happened, Ibyang?

415
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:02,873
Why are your steps
wrong again?

416
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:06,960
Because it's really hard,
and so fast!

417
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:09,922
And why are we practicing

418
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:11,632
with just the two of us?

419
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:14,218
Because we need to double
our effort,

420
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:16,720
so Hailey won't scold us.

421
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:18,430
Especially you.

422
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:21,183
Don't be like that,
I'm just concerned about you.

423
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:23,352
[soft drama music playing]

424
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:26,563
I wish Big Sister Tonet was here,

425
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:29,024
she's good at teaching.

426
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:31,902
Wow. So I'm not?

427
00:18:33,028 --> 00:18:34,363
I didn't say anything.

428
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:37,324
[music continues]

429
00:18:37,407 --> 00:18:38,408
Surprise!

430
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:39,326
[chuckles]
Oh, oh, oh.

431
00:18:39,409 --> 00:18:40,077
Tatoy!

432
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,245
Daddy!

433
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:42,663
Oh, no “Mommy”?

434
00:18:42,746 --> 00:18:43,288
No, Mommy.

435
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:44,873
“Daddy”-- just “Daddy,”
really?

436
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:46,125
Hmm! Just kidding!

437
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,084
What are you doing?

438
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:50,963
Ah, we're practicing for the
dance club audition.

439
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:53,966
Audrey: Did you know that there's
a special guest

440
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:57,136
who will watch your
practice today?

441
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:58,178
Special guest?

442
00:18:58,262 --> 00:18:59,429
Atoy: Mmm-hmm.

443
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:00,556
Who could it be?

444
00:19:01,181 --> 00:19:03,183
Daddy's friend, Mommy's friend?

445
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,853
[light music playing]

446
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:07,146
Hello, kids!

447
00:19:07,229 --> 00:19:09,064
[chuckles]

448
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,691
Both: Uncle Oka!

449
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:12,317
Hey. Hey, hey. Easy, easy.

450
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:13,652
Hi, Ibyang! Hi, Janine!

451
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:15,279
[Oscar chuckles]

452
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:16,655
Wait.

453
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,198
You're back.

454
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:19,783
So, does that mean…

455
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:22,536
you're really going to
live here now?!

456
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:23,871
[chuckles]

457
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:25,914
It means, you're right!

458
00:19:25,998 --> 00:19:27,207
Ibyang: Oh, whoa!

459
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:28,500
Thanks to your parents!

460
00:19:30,210 --> 00:19:32,838
Ah, Oscar, what do you
want to eat?

461
00:19:32,921 --> 00:19:34,673
So I can just cook that.

462
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:38,135
Me, me anything is fine, ah--

463
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,928
Whatever Atoy's favorite is,

464
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:40,679
that's also mine.

465
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:42,139
Ahh.

466
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:44,433
So pakbet Ilocano with
bagoong isda?

467
00:19:44,975 --> 00:19:45,767
ATOY: Of course!

468
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:47,561
Oh, Love, did I tell you?

469
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:51,523
Oka makes the most delicious pakbet
in the camp back then,

470
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:53,734
that's why it became my favorite.

471
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:56,236
Oh, just admit that you were just
very hungry back then,

472
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,655
so whatever you cook for him,
it would taste good.

473
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:01,200
[chuckling]

474
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:04,620
[heavy music playing]

475
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:06,830
Emerson, don't be in a bad
mood anymore!

476
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,082
We have a new mission, look!

477
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:10,876
Miss Siony was here earlier!

478
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:12,878
She says she's missing some
fish! There, look!

479
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,173
Dried milkfish?

480
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:17,090
Paldo: Yes.

481
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:18,550
[pleasant music playing]

482
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:19,885
Unbelievable.

483
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:25,182
Don't we have any other more pointless
case than what we have now?

484
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,184
Hey, you’re over the line.

485
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:28,894
It's Miss Siony, though!

486
00:20:28,977 --> 00:20:30,854
And it's good that someone
trusts us, you know.

487
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:32,606
[music fades…]

488
00:20:32,689 --> 00:20:34,066
What's going on between
you and Miss Siony?

489
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,525
Why does it seem like
she trusts you?

490
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:36,276
Karla: Brother Emerson!

491
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,611
Brother, Brother Emerson!

492
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:38,779
Oh?

493
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:41,448
- It's Uno!
- Emerson: What?

494
00:20:41,531 --> 00:20:42,616
Uno is missing!

495
00:20:43,283 --> 00:20:44,534
He escaped from the hospital,

496
00:20:44,618 --> 00:20:45,786
before Samir could
get him!

497
00:20:45,869 --> 00:20:48,580
[suspicious music playing]

498
00:20:49,539 --> 00:20:52,292
O-M-G!

499
00:20:54,002 --> 00:20:55,504
Emerson: I think this is it.

500
00:20:56,171 --> 00:21:00,342
This is our one big, big,
big-time break.

501
00:21:00,884 --> 00:21:02,511
This is our big-time mission.

502
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:05,264
O.H.U.

503
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:08,183
Operation Hanap Uno (Operation Find Uno)!

504
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:12,896
Let’s plan how we'll find Uno.

505
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:13,897
Right.

506
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:15,357
What's the plan?

507
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:19,069
Let’s think about it.

508
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:21,238
Emerson: I'll think, I haven't thought
of anything yet.

509
00:21:21,863 --> 00:21:22,990
But, you see--

510
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:25,993
It's not easy to look for
a missing tracker.

511
00:21:26,618 --> 00:21:27,536
And we're not in a hurry.

512
00:21:27,619 --> 00:21:28,787
Are we in a hurry?

513
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:30,831
[sneaky music playing]

514
00:21:30,914 --> 00:21:33,041
You know, just update me,

515
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:34,209
just text me, okay.

516
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:35,252
Wait, wait, wait.

517
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:36,962
[music continues]

518
00:21:37,045 --> 00:21:38,463
Besides being a firefighter,

519
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:41,341
what else do we know
about Uno?

520
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:43,427
[suspicious music playing]

521
00:21:43,510 --> 00:21:46,388
Maybe you should ask
Brother Atoy.

522
00:21:46,471 --> 00:21:49,766
[music continues]

523
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:51,768
[music fades]

524
00:21:51,852 --> 00:21:52,477
Atoy: Hmm.

525
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:53,854
Mmm-hmm.

526
00:21:53,937 --> 00:21:54,980
That smells so good, Love.

527
00:21:55,063 --> 00:21:56,732
What is this you're cooking, huh?

528
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:57,691
Oh, it really smells good,

529
00:21:57,774 --> 00:21:59,609
because it's delicious.

530
00:21:59,693 --> 00:22:00,485
Taste it. Go on.

531
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:02,070
Wow. Okay, okay.

532
00:22:02,154 --> 00:22:03,155
Hmm, it really is delicious!

533
00:22:03,572 --> 00:22:05,240
Not me!

534
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:05,824
No, taste this--

535
00:22:05,907 --> 00:22:06,491
Well, that's really--

536
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:07,117
Oh, okay.

537
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,076
Let me taste, let me taste.

538
00:22:08,994 --> 00:22:09,745
It's still hot.

539
00:22:09,828 --> 00:22:11,371
[light music playing]

540
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:12,039
Hmm…

541
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:12,914
[smooches]

542
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:14,291
That's too much, more--

543
00:22:14,374 --> 00:22:15,667
Okay, fine, I'll taste this now.

544
00:22:15,751 --> 00:22:16,960
All right.

545
00:22:17,044 --> 00:22:19,171
Hmm, the broth is delicious.

546
00:22:19,254 --> 00:22:20,422
Hmm…

547
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:22,215
It's your favorite.

548
00:22:22,299 --> 00:22:23,425
Of course.

549
00:22:23,508 --> 00:22:24,760
My Love is really so kind.

550
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,678
Right? Oh, you!

551
00:22:27,095 --> 00:22:29,139
Audrey: I can't finish cooking.

552
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:30,098
It’s all right, I'll help you.

553
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:30,891
Oh okay, okay, okay.

554
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:33,185
Wait for about 10 minutes, and--

555
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:35,187
[pan sizzling nearby]

556
00:22:36,396 --> 00:22:37,272
[gasps]

557
00:22:37,355 --> 00:22:37,898
Oh--

558
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:39,232
Audrey: Ah, Oscar.

559
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:41,193
Sorry.
[clears throat]

560
00:22:41,276 --> 00:22:41,818
How are you?

561
00:22:41,902 --> 00:22:42,861
Oscar: Ah, no--

562
00:22:42,944 --> 00:22:44,863
I'm the one disturbing your…

563
00:22:44,946 --> 00:22:45,697
lovey-dovey time.

564
00:22:45,781 --> 00:22:46,740
[chuckles softly]

565
00:22:47,365 --> 00:22:48,241
Sorry, sorry.

566
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:50,994
Ah, how about you?

567
00:22:51,078 --> 00:22:54,956
Uhm, did you leave behind
a girlfriend or wife?

568
00:22:55,582 --> 00:22:56,208
Uhm…

569
00:22:56,291 --> 00:22:57,584
[clears throat]

570
00:22:57,667 --> 00:22:58,418
No. Yes, yes.

571
00:22:58,502 --> 00:22:59,544
It's, ah, Mary Ann.

572
00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:00,504
My former girlfriend.

573
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:03,632
But I’m sure she's moved
on by now.

574
00:23:03,715 --> 00:23:05,050
Mmm-hmm. She has someone else.

575
00:23:05,550 --> 00:23:07,302
I was gone for 10 years,
after all.

576
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:10,680
You know, you really can't say

577
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:12,891
unless you go see Mary Ann.

578
00:23:13,391 --> 00:23:15,560
Because, us, you know.

579
00:23:15,644 --> 00:23:17,979
It took more than 8 years before
we saw each other again.

580
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:20,357
Audrey: But by the grace of God,

581
00:23:21,024 --> 00:23:22,901
we were really the ones
destined for each other.

582
00:23:23,401 --> 00:23:24,236
[chuckles softly]

583
00:23:25,487 --> 00:23:26,196
[pensive music playing]

584
00:23:26,279 --> 00:23:27,489
Yeah, uhm…

585
00:23:27,572 --> 00:23:29,116
my type is different now
too, you know.

586
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:30,408
[music swells]

587
00:23:30,492 --> 00:23:31,118
You.

588
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:32,452
[music fades]

589
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:34,329
Maybe you have…

590
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:36,206
Someone you can set
me up with.

591
00:23:36,915 --> 00:23:38,250
Maybe you have
a sister, Audrey.

592
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:39,167
Audrey: Uhm…

593
00:23:40,752 --> 00:23:43,505
Ah, no. Audrey has
no sister.

594
00:23:44,047 --> 00:23:46,299
[suspenseful music playing]

595
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:47,384
What a pity.

596
00:23:47,467 --> 00:23:49,886
[music swells]

597
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:56,935
[electronic blipping]

598
00:23:57,727 --> 00:24:00,230
[intense music playing]

599
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:01,565
Why did you let Oscar come back?

600
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:02,983
Emerson: I just couldn't
tell you but…

601
00:24:03,066 --> 00:24:05,068
I think he's kind of not good,
you know.

602
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:06,278
Everything is clear to me now.

603
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:07,571
There are…

604
00:24:07,654 --> 00:24:11,741
good things I want to happen
in my life.

605
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:14,161
I’ll make sure all of those
happen, Audrey.

606
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:16,538
Just one mistake

607
00:24:16,621 --> 00:24:17,998
and we're all eliminated.

608
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:19,291
I practiced.

609
00:24:19,374 --> 00:24:21,501
I won't make a mistake,
promise.

610
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:23,920
I don't want to be eliminated
because of Ibyang!

611
00:24:24,379 --> 00:24:25,714
I have a lead on Uno's location.

612
00:24:25,797 --> 00:24:27,966
'Toy, Uno is wounded,

613
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:29,384
he needs our help.

614
00:24:29,467 --> 00:24:30,677
Okay, okay, okay, okay.
I'll go there.

615
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:31,928
Send me the address.

616
00:24:32,345 --> 00:24:33,471
[“Mamang Sastre” playing]

617
00:24:33,555 --> 00:24:35,223
Oh? Have you seen
the footage

618
00:24:35,307 --> 00:24:36,892
that I asked from you?

619
00:24:36,975 --> 00:24:38,643
[music continues…]

620
00:24:38,727 --> 00:24:40,103
Uhm… [clears throat]

621
00:24:40,729 --> 00:24:42,856
[music swells]
